./docs/build_notes.md:26:- Sixth-publisher research (2026-10-15): found Engineering.com's artificial-intelligence category RSS at `https://www.engineering.com/category/technology/artificial-intelligence/feed/`, fetched and parsed it as a real feed with ten dated entries inside the 45-day window. Its three newest entries are dated 2026-09-30, 2026-09-23, and 2026-09-22. The September 30 "Welcome to the vibe-CAD era" article is especially relevant because the author reports personally testing Backflip's photo/video/drawing-to-CAD modes and records both successes and failures, rather than only repeating a release claim. Added this feed to live `config/sources.json` under distinct producer `engineering-com`; editorial selection must still decide whether each article is accepted. The feed prepends whitespace before its XML declaration, which the finder tolerated but the collector rejected; `collectors/fetch_feeds.py` now strips that leading whitespace before XML parsing. The actual collector parser then returned the expected top three dated articles. Configuration (6), examples (12), and feed-finder (18) tests pass, and the collector compiles. The old saved run has not collected this source, so it still has only five accepted publishers. Also considered Flow Engineering's 2026-09-30 announcement, but its blog did not yield a verified RSS/Atom feed and its release is primarily a company claim; it was not added.
