./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-d2957a1764744192bbd015903695b12a-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151286\",\"version_id\":\"a393edb1af792a0f22f58a9c9be7640474dbeb4ed41d7ec336f5428b607cf2bc\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh and highly relevant CAD/PLM coverage, but it is an Autodesk executive interview about features expected in future quarters rather than a check of released capability. The productivity, adoption, and agentic-PLM claims are vendor claims with no disclosed tasks, accuracy, failure cases, or independent evaluation. A released workflow and reproducible evidence of how it extracts and validates PLM information would make it checkable.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151329\",\"version_id\":\"a5a6e64fd4f2a87b5b45be5afd0c01d19fd3ee1e8b8f12be9e7e49964e03d82b\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"The item is fresh and relevant to CAD-to-simulation workflows, and it clearly distinguishes Comsol's upcoming release from a released product. However, the SimScale agent's claim that it can repair simulation-readiness, choose setups, mesh, run physics, and report results comes from SimScale's press release, with no disclosed cases or verification of result quality. The Autodesk material repeats the same underlying AU announcement covered elsewhere and is not independent corroboration.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh, directly relevant CAD evidence with a named practitioner test and checkable outcomes: the author imported Backflip STEP outputs into Fusion, applied the specified material, and verified exact mass for two TooTallToby drawing challenges. It also records meaningful failure conditions: a Fusion feature-tree import was incomplete and the system produced only one of seven bodies on a multibody drawing. The tests establish success on two constrained benchmark-style drawings, not general accuracy, manufacturability, or reliable reconstruction from photos and video.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This fresh first-party announcement documents a currently testable, opt-in Onshape Labs feature: AI-generated descriptions of static model thumbnails are searchable for public documents only. The publisher explicitly limits the scope and labels internal-data, supplier-catalog, reuse, and cost-reduction scenarios as speculative, which keeps the claim appropriately bounded. It is useful commercial perspective, though evidence from working engineers and private datasets remains missing.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/featurescript-mcp-server-use-cases-text-code-cad\",\"version_id\":\"9656a0a35f95ac0e0adb6ba1530e2759342633cbcecba8de9948699a032ab5a8\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"The FeatureScript MCP Server is relevant to text-to-code-to-CAD, but this vendor use-case article provides illustrative scenarios rather than observed outcomes. Claims that an LLM can preserve parametric intent, manufacturing accuracy, optimize code, or integrate analysis have no stated model, prompts, test models, graders, failure rate, or independent check. Reproducible examples showing generated FeatureScript passing geometry and standards checks would settle the central claims.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:173f6c2b-e1b8-4de0-b7b7-4b15658d52e6\",\"version_id\":\"da6be0ed10587e503de7706e1ad94cd3d0409d0c4664a004a631d6f27c500a73\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"Although fresh and timestamped, this episode concerns narrative intelligence, coaching, and human identity rather than 3D modeling, CAD, geometry, simulation-ready assets, or physical-system verification. It supplies personal perspectives rather than checkable technical evidence relevant to the publication's audience. It therefore fails the relevance criterion.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:509842f7-f592-432c-b01a-ad26a2ae1e31\",\"version_id\":\"122e3cc3de2a41fbd9f0de08a089614db628a34697f00a720e1d3abf5b405dca\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This fresh, timestamped discussion is about general education in an AI-driven world, not frontier 3D modeling, CAD, or physical AI. Its brief reference to mechanical engineering does not provide a capability, geometry, simulation, or verification claim that would help technical product managers make build decisions. It fails the relevance criterion.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d\",\"version_id\":\"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"The episode is fresh and relevant robotics context because it discusses world simulation and the different sensor constraints of physical systems. But it is an NVIDIA executive interview, and the sampled automatic transcript supplies no checkable experiment, deployment result, disclosed evaluation conditions, or independently verified claim. Audio-confirmed passages plus released model, data, and transfer evaluation details would be needed before accepting it.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/008\",\"version_id\":\"1cb4eefeb597341d29e650ad7c122c9eea10b1aa146aef9c4a6214acdf2c2983\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh and promising robotics context for piece 2 because it explicitly distinguishes simulation ranking from real-arm evidence and reports a purported blind evaluation with stated task and attempt counts. However, the numerical and attributional details appear only in an automatic transcript and must be checked against the audio and underlying Black Forest Labs, Positronic Robotics, and leaderboard materials. The reported external test was commissioned by the model developer, so even if confirmed it is not independent corroboration of broad deployment performance.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/009\",\"version_id\":\"13aaf6bfc525bce0b9a1887162b0c0c3d4dd024b9bafd1c223a5bc48bd063692\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh, relevant supporting robotics coverage that frames generalization and autonomy in terms of held-out tasks, interventions, simulation, and a real-robot result. Yet the reported 70%, 6%, and 10% results, as well as the code-and-weights claim, are taken from an automatic transcript and require confirmation against the audio and cited Tsinghua paper and repository. Even as described, most evidence is simulation and the physical result is one task, so it does not establish general physical transfer.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-01-609a51c3edc7488fa618a125c8d38d12-attempt-2.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"From CAD Drafts to Connected Workflows—With Checks Still Doing the Real Work\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"The meaningful shift is not that frontier models can generate geometry, but that they are entering CAD workflows as editable drafts, search layers, and connected automation. The strongest near-term value is in bounded tasks with explicit checks—such as mass verification or searchable public thumbnails—while simulation and agentic workflow demonstrations remain useful infrastructure signals rather than proof of dependable physical or production outcomes.\",\"synthesis\":\"Engineering.com supplies a practitioner check of drawing-to-CAD outputs, while Onshape documents a narrowly available retrieval feature and the survey places both within a broader pattern: models can produce useful editable artifacts, but engineering requirements still need separate verification. Nvidia's simulation-ready workflow reinforces the same boundary: visual, physics, and grasp checks are distinct stages, so a CAD-to-simulation pipeline should preserve those checks instead of treating an imported asset as physically faithful by default. The added analysis is a deployment distinction: adopt AI first where the artifact can be checked against a task-specific criterion, and treat connected or simulated workflows as scaffolding for later validation rather than as autonomy evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The practitioner CAD test covers two constrained drawing challenges and one multibody failure, not tolerances, manufacturability, or representative production drawings. Onshape's feature is opt-in and limited to public documents, while the Nvidia workflow is a vendor demonstration without a reported hardware-transfer experiment.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"A practitioner test found that Backflip drawing-to-CAD outputs had exact mass on two TooTallToby drawing challenges after STEP import into Fusion and material assignment, but the system generated only one of seven bodies on a multibody drawing.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"I was able to import it into Fusion, apply the material, and check the mass. I won’t give away the answer (you can check it yourself on TooTallToby.com) but I can verify that Backflip got it exactly correct.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"And once again, Backflip aced the test.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"This time, Backflip failed, and obviously—it only created one of the seven bodies, though as far as I could tell, it was correct.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Onshape's AI-Generated Thumbnail Description Search is an opt-in Onshape Labs feature for public documents that makes AI-written descriptions of static model thumbnails searchable.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"AI-Generated Thumbnail Description Search is an opt-in Onshape Labs feature that generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"It applies to public documents only, not your private data (yet).\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"The current public record supports frontier models as first-draft tools for editable 3D and CAD artifacts, but not as evidence that outputs meet tolerance or manufacturability requirements.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Only 132 cases include runnable code, so most capabilities below are demonstrated rather than independently reproduced.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"They may have been simplistic, made to be modeled and lacking the dust and difficulty of real shop drawings.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"Nvidia's demonstrated CAD-to-simulation workflow separates visual-reference checks, physics-property setup, and grasp-oriented simulation checks, so it does not itself establish that a generated asset will transfer faithfully to hardware.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"a few such controllers have run on physical arms and hands, though none has been tested under conditions withheld during development\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/briefs_reviewed.jsonl:1:{"piece_id":"01","title":"CAD AI Is Moving Into Workflows—But Its Checks Still Define Its Value","question":"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?","argument":"This month’s meaningful change is not simply AI-generated geometry, but its entry into recognizable CAD workflows: reconstructing some constrained parts, making model appearances searchable, and linking design data across applications. The strongest evidence supports bounded first-draft and retrieval uses, not autonomous engineering decisions. For technical leaders, the near-term opportunity is to deploy AI where a matching CAD, geometry, or workflow check can reject errors before release.","synthesis":"The evidence shows movement from isolated generation toward tool-connected CAD work, but with sharply different validation boundaries. Engineering.com used a specified-material mass check on two exported CAD outputs; Onshape describes searchable text derived from model thumbnails in public documents; and Cadalyst reports that Autodesk’s connected-workflow announcements span available, preview, and planned functions. Nvidia’s sim-ready workflow similarly separates visual, physics, and grasp checks, while robotics reporting shows why a completed action sequence is not itself evidence of task success. The resulting editorial conclusion is that adoption readiness depends less on whether a model produces an artifact than on whether the organization has an acceptance check that matches the consequence of using it.","limitations":"The evidence does not establish dependable performance on production drawings, tolerances, manufacturability, private engineering repositories, or end-to-end change approval. Backflip’s strongest reconstruction evidence comes from one practitioner’s two successful benchmark-style mass checks; Onshape and Autodesk provide vendor or event-reporting evidence rather than independent production-deployment results. The robotics evidence is supporting context, not proof that CAD-generated or simulation-ready assets transfer reliably to hardware.","claims":[{"claim_id":"01-c1","statement":"A practitioner reported that two Backflip drawing-to-CAD STEP outputs matched the required mass after material assignment in Fusion, while Backflip produced only one body for a seven-body drawing.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"apply the material and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"verify that Backflip got it exactly correct"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"once again, Backflip aced the test"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"only created one of the seven bodies"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c2","statement":"Onshape says its opt-in Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from static model thumbnails and currently applies only to public documents.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search","version_id":"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search","version_id":"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"currently applies to public documents"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c3","statement":"Cadalyst reported that Autodesk showed developing Fusion agentic-PLM capabilities and distinguished current capabilities from beta, Tech Preview, and longer-term work.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Fusion’s developing agentic PLM capabilities"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Some are in beta or Tech Preview"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"longer-term direction"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c4","statement":"For CAD teams, the defensible near-term adoption pattern is to use AI for first drafts or retrieval only when a task-appropriate downstream check and approval process can catch errors.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"apply the material and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0005"}},{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010","version_id":"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0036"}}]}]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/briefs_reviewed.jsonl:2:{"piece_id":"02","title":"What Agentic CAD’s Checks Actually Prove","question":"Which claims withstand scrutiny, and where are the evidence or interpretations in tension?","argument":"Current evidence supports agentic CAD as a useful first-draft tool for bounded geometry tasks with explicit downstream checks, not as a replacement for engineering validation. An Engineering.com practitioner verified two Backflip STEP outputs by mass in Fusion, but also found incomplete native-CAD imports and a multibody failure. NVIDIA’s workflow separates visual, physics, and grasp checks; the broader record shows why none alone proves tolerances, manufacturability, or physical transfer.","synthesis":"The useful change is not that generated geometry can look plausible, but that some workflows now expose it to distinct checks. Engineering.com’s material-and-mass test checks two outputs against a constrained drawing criterion, while NVIDIA identifies separate checks for appearance, configured physics, and simulated grasping. Connecting these with the MIT survey yields a practical rule: retain editable artifacts and match each deployment claim to a relevant check, rather than treating a valid import, a visual match, or a simulation pass as interchangeable evidence.","limitations":"The Backflip assessment covers three TooTallToby drawings and does not report repeated trials; its two successful checks do not establish performance on production drawings, tolerances, or manufacturability. NVIDIA’s workflow is a vendor demonstration, not an independently replicated physical-transfer study. The podcast evidence is an automatic transcript, so its RobotWorld figures remain a source-reported result here rather than independently verified evidence.","claims":[{"claim_id":"02-c1","statement":"An Engineering.com practitioner imported Backflip STEP outputs into Fusion, applied material, checked mass, and reported two drawing-to-CAD outputs as exactly correct.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"import it into Fusion, apply the material, and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"I can verify that Backflip got it exactly correct."}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"once again, Backflip aced the test."}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c2","statement":"The observed import defects and seven-body failure mean that the two mass checks cannot establish reliable native-CAD reconstruction or multibody performance.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Only a partial version of the part was imported"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"it only created one of the seven bodies"}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c3","statement":"NVIDIA presents its CAD-to-simulation process as distinct visual-reference, physics-property, and grasp-oriented checks.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0004"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0005"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0006"}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c4","statement":"The available evidence supports treating model outputs as first drafts that require tolerance and manufacturability checks before final engineering use.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"budget for tolerance, structural and manufacturability checks"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"They may have been simplistic"}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c5","statement":"The podcast reports that five models were run once on each RobotWorld task and that 63 tasks went unsolved by all of them.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010","version_id":"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0040"}},{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010","version_id":"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0047"}},{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010","version_id":"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0072"}}]}]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/briefs_reviewed.jsonl:3:{"piece_id":"03","title":"From CAD Generation to Governed Verification","question":"What do these developments imply for the audience, and what should they watch next?","argument":"AI-assisted CAD is becoming useful for bounded drafting and retrieval tasks, but technical leaders should treat verification and workflow governance—not generation—as the near-term implementation problem. The strongest evidence supports using models to create or find editable design artifacts, then checking the properties that matter in native tools or simulations. Connected CAD platforms and simulation pipelines increase the value of those checks, but neither a live demo nor a passed simulation sequence establishes manufacturability or physical-world reliability.","synthesis":"Engineering.com provides a concrete example of CAD output checked by imported STEP geometry and material mass, while the MIT survey explains why results characterize a model-plus-harness system and do not establish tolerance or manufacturability. Autodesk’s connected-workflow direction and Onshape’s limited public-document search feature suggest that AI will increasingly operate across engineering data rather than only inside a modeling command. Nvidia’s CAD-to-simulation walkthrough adds a verification ladder—visual, physics, sim-ready, then full sequence—while the RobotWorld discussion keeps the distinction between simulated task outcomes and dependable embodied performance visible. The practical implication is to build around explicit approval gates, preserved native artifacts, and checks matched to the decision being automated.","limitations":"The accepted evidence does not include independent longitudinal studies of working engineering teams using connected CAD workflows on private production data. The Backflip test verifies two constrained drawing-to-CAD cases, while Autodesk and Nvidia primarily document vendor demonstrations or workflows rather than general production reliability; the podcast’s automated transcript is also not an independently verified source for its reported figures.","claims":[{"claim_id":"03-c1","statement":"A practitioner verified exact mass for two Backflip drawing-to-CAD outputs after importing their STEP files into Fusion and applying the specified material.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"import it into Fusion, apply the material, and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Backflip got it exactly correct"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Backflip aced the test"}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c2","statement":"The two mass checks establish mass agreement for those drawings, not tolerance conformance or manufacturability.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"lacking the dust and difficulty of real shop drawings"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"benchmark results characterize complete model and harness systems"}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c3","statement":