./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-1bb39f96d56842fb9a97485ea497c5a7-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151286\",\"version_id\":\"a393edb1af792a0f22f58a9c9be7640474dbeb4ed41d7ec336f5428b607cf2bc\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"This is timely and relevant CAD/PLM coverage, but the central agentic-PLM capability is an Autodesk executive’s future-oriented claim: it is due in coming quarters and no released workflow, accuracy check, or customer result is described. The interview provides a citable timestamped passage but not evidence of what the agent can reliably extract from unstructured communications or how its PLM updates are verified.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151329\",\"version_id\":\"a5a6e64fd4f2a87b5b45be5afd0c01d19fd3ee1e8b8f12be9e7e49964e03d82b\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"The SimScale-on-Onshape integration is relevant, but its claim that one prompt can repair simulation readiness, choose a setup, mesh, run physics, and report results is attributed to SimScale’s press release, with no disclosed models, test cases, solver settings, or validation against known answers. The Comsol release is also prospective rather than a checkable release result, while this Engineering.com item should not count as independent corroboration of the linked vendor announcements.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is a fresh, unusually checkable practitioner test of a CAD capability: the author imported Backflip STEP outputs into Fusion, assigned the specified material, and verified exact mass for two TooTallToby drawing challenges, while reporting a seven-body failure and Fusion add-in discrepancies. It supports drawing-to-CAD feasibility only on these bounded benchmark-style parts, not general manufacturability or dimensional accuracy from photos; the CEO’s broader adoption claims remain source claims.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is a timely, relevant commercial CAD release with a concrete and bounded mechanism: descriptions are generated from existing thumbnails and indexed for search, and the article explicitly says it is opt-in, experimental, and limited to public documents. It is vendor reporting and provides no retrieval-quality evaluation, so claims about reducing duplicate designs or extending to private and supplier data are speculative rather than demonstrated.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/featurescript-mcp-server-use-cases-text-code-cad\",\"version_id\":\"9656a0a35f95ac0e0adb6ba1530e2759342633cbcecba8de9948699a032ab5a8\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"The FeatureScript MCP server is relevant to text-to-code CAD, but this vendor article mainly presents hypothetical use cases and broad assertions that generated features preserve parametric intent, manufacturing accuracy, and analysis quality. It supplies no reproducible examples, generated code, pass/fail geometry checks, standards-validation results, or failure rates; those are the missing evidence needed to assess the capability.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:173f6c2b-e1b8-4de0-b7b7-4b15658d52e6\",\"version_id\":\"da6be0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This timestamped podcast concerns narrative intelligence, coaching, and human identity in AI rather than 3D modeling, CAD, geometry, simulation-ready assets, or physical-system verification. Its general reflections do not provide a relevant technical development or checkable evidence for the publication’s audience.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:509842f7-f592-432c-b01a-ad26a2ae1e31\",\"version_id\":\"122e3cc3de2a41fbd9f0de08a089614db628a34697f00a720e1d3abf5b405dca\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"Although current and timestamped, this is a general discussion of education in an AI-driven world, not an item about CAD, 3D modeling, or physical AI capability. A passing reference to mechanical engineering does not establish relevance or offer evidence that would help engineering leaders evaluate frontier physical-system tools.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d\",\"version_id\":\"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282\",\"decision\":\"defer\",\"reason\":\"This is relevant robotics context, especially its discussion of world simulation and varied robot sensors, but it is an NVIDIA executive interview rather than an independent evaluation of open physical-AI models. The retained automatic transcript supplies timestamps but cannot independently verify its technical claims; released artifacts, benchmark conditions, and physical-transfer results would be needed.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/008\",\"version_id\":\"1cb4eefeb597341d29e650ad7c122c9eea10b1aa146aef9c4a6214acdf2c2983\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is timely supporting robotics coverage that explicitly distinguishes a 120-task simulation leaderboard from real-arm evidence, then reports a blinded external-arm evaluation with ten tasks, three attempts each, a common time window, scoring sheet, and video. The numerical claims remain reported through an automatically transcribed secondary podcast and the evaluation was commissioned by the winning vendor, so it is useful chiefly for the scrutiny framework and pending direct inspection of the video and underlying results.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/009\",\"version_id\":\"13aaf6bfc525bce0b9a1887162b0c0c3d4dd024b9bafd1c223a5bc48bd063692\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This fresh supporting-robotics item directly addresses what was checked: it contrasts simulated generalization with one held-out real-robot task, flags that the paper is five days old, and notes code and weights are available for replication. It also frames intervention rate as a more decision-relevant operational measure than per-task success, while its reported percentages and startup autonomy claim remain unverified transcript-derived reporting rather than independent proof.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"02\",\"03\"]}"}}
