./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_checked.jsonl:10:{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh, timestamped survey directly addresses the lead topics and states its evidence boundary: 1,646 public posts across 707 cases were checked against available code, video, and documentation, while only 132 cases provide runnable code. It separates editable-scene and parametric-CAD benchmark results from untested tolerance and manufacturability claims, and separates simulation/controller results from withheld-condition physical validation. The survey is valuable research synthesis, though its aggregated claims remain only as strong as the linked case-level checks and it does not replace independent customer or working-engineer evidence.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_checked.jsonl:18:{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282","decision":"reject","reason":"The episode is relevant robotics context, but its physical-AI claims are presented in an interview with an NVIDIA vice president and lack a disclosed experiment, evaluation protocol, or independent replication in the supplied passages. Timestamped automatic-transcript statements about open models and world simulation are source claims, not verification of robot performance. It would add vendor perspective without a checkable result for the audience to assess.","piece_ids":[]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/content-write_video_scripts-sh-e4245da4f08f41a58fb7c183c8be00d3-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"markdown\":\"## Scene 1 — The answer\\n\\n**Narration:** What changed for CAD teams? AI is moving into recognizable workflows: reconstructing some constrained parts, making model appearances searchable, and linking design data across applications. The evidence supports checked first drafts and retrieval. It does not support autonomous engineering decisions. This is a reported assessment, as of October 16, 2026. This video uses AI-generated presentation.\\n\\n**Visual:** Title card. Three workflow lanes: “Reconstruct,” “Search,” and “Connect.” Under them: “Checked first drafts and retrieval” versus “Not autonomous approval.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** Agentic 3D, “CAD AI Is Moving Into Workflows—But Its Checks Still Define Its Value,” October 16, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 2 — The core test\\n\\n**Narration:** The central question is simple: what was actually checked, by whom, and under what conditions? A valid solid does not prove a part is manufacturable. A good-looking result does not prove dimensions are right. And a completed action sequence does not prove the task succeeded.\\n\\n**Visual:** A labeled gate diagram: “AI output” flows to “Task-appropriate check,” then “Approval.” Red callouts: “Appearance is not dimensions,” “Solid is not manufacturability,” “Action is not task success.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c4 — MIT Computational Design and Fabrication Group, “On the Opportunities and Risks of Frontier Models for 3D Modeling, Computational Design and Robotics,” September 22, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 3 — Drawing to CAD: a bounded check\\n\\n**Narration:** Engineering.com reported a concrete Backflip test. A practitioner exported two drawing-to-CAD results as STEP files, imported them into Fusion, assigned the specified material, and found that both matched the required mass. That is a reported fact.\\n\\nThe check observed aggregate solid volume with the specified material for those two drawings. It did not check feature history, tolerances, manufacturing intent, or body count.\\n\\n**Visual:** Split screen: drawing to Backflip to STEP to Fusion. A green badge: “Check observed: specified material + required mass.” A gray list: “Not checked: tolerances, manufacturability, editable feature history.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c1 — Engineering.com, “Welcome to the vibe-CAD era,” September 30, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 4 — The failure matters\\n\\n**Narration:** The same practitioner reported a multibody wire-shelf failure. Backflip produced only one body for a seven-body drawing. So two successful mass checks are evidence for checked first drafts on constrained parts. They are not a general reliability rate for production drawings.\\n\\n**Visual:** “7 bodies claimed” beside “1 body produced.” Keep the mass-check badge visible, with a label: “Different check needed: body count.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c1 — Engineering.com, “Welcome to the vibe-CAD era,” September 30, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 5 — Search is a different capability\\n\\n**Narration:** Onshape says its opt-in Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from static model thumbnails. It currently applies only to public documents. This is a source claim, not an independent deployment result.\\n\\nThat supports a narrow retrieval claim: users can search visible characteristics alongside metadata. It does not establish consistently accurate descriptions, reduced duplicate work, or performance on private engineering repositories.\\n\\n**Visual:** A public-document thumbnail becomes the searchable phrase “red bracket.” Labels: “Observed scope: static thumbnails, public documents.” “Check to add: relevance and duplicate-work reduction.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c2 — Onshape, “Introducing AI Descriptive Image Search from Onshape Labs,” October 5, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 6 — Connected workflows are not yet proof\\n\\n**Narration:** Cadalyst reported that Autodesk showed developing Fusion agentic-PLM capabilities. It also distinguished current capabilities from beta, Tech Preview, and longer-term work. That is evidence of product direction and connected workflow design. It is not evidence of production reliability in a customer’s data.\\n\\nFor PLM, the downstream checks should cover permissions, data provenance, and change approval.\\n\\n**Visual:** Workflow diagram: “Shortage” to “Approved substitute” to “Change order,” with status tags: “Available,” “Beta,” “Tech Preview,” “Longer-term.” Approval gate labels: permissions, provenance, approval.\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c3 — Cadalyst, “Autodesk University 2026: What the Announcements Mean for CAD Teams,” September 25, 2026.\\n\\n## Scene 7 — Supporting lesson from simulation and robotics\\n\\n**Narration:** NVIDIA separates visual checks from physics checks, then tests grasps in simulation. Its video says to check scale, parts, and appearance against references; then joints, collision geometry, and physical properties; then rerun foundation checks and grasp tests after fixes.\\n\\nA visual pass does not establish plausible physics. A simulated grasp does not prove hardware performance. Separately, the Physical AI Podcast describes a program checking whether a commanded job got done. Performing actions is not the same as achieving the task.\\n\\n**Visual:** Three stacked checks: “Visual: scale, parts, appearance,” “Physics: joints, collision geometry, physical properties,” “Simulation: grasp test.” End with “Hardware transfer: not established.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c4 — NVIDIA, “5 Steps to Create SimReady Assets for Robotics with Frontier AI Models,” October 8, 2026, 00:20–00:47. Physical AI Podcast, “AI Models Fail 63 of 84 Robot Tasks, Waymo Borrows $5B,” October 10, 2026, 02:23–02:27.\\n\\n## Scene 8 — Startup watch and what to do next\\n\\n**Narration:** Cableteque announced expansion of its wire-harness quoting platform to Europe. It said European customer data could be hosted in AWS Europe Central as of September 30, 2026. That is a company claim and a market signal, not a verified extraction-accuracy result or customer-outcome study.\\n\\nFor leaders, start with a workflow you can check before release. Define the acceptance check before choosing the tool. For drawings, check mass, body count, dimensions, and tolerances. For search, measure relevance and duplicate-work prevention. For PLM, test permissions, provenance, and approvals. Watch next for published task sets, reproducible scoring, private-data tests, and tolerance and manufacturability checks.\\n\\n**Visual:** Final checklist: “Define check,” “Run downstream validation,” “Require approval,” “Log failures by type.” Cableteque card labeled “Market signal; accuracy not independently established.”\\n\\n**Source on screen:** 01-c5 — Cableteque, “Cableteque Brings AI-Powered Wire Harness Quoting Platform to Europe,” September 29, 2026.\\n\\n**Video description**\\n\\nArticle: [ARTICLE LINK]\\n\\nReferences: Engineering.com, “Welcome to the vibe-CAD era,” September 30, 2026; Onshape, “Introducing AI Descriptive Image Search from Onshape Labs,” October 5, 2026; Cadalyst, “Autodesk University 2026: What the Announcements Mean for CAD Teams,” September 25, 2026; MIT Computational Design and Fabrication Group, “On the Opportunities and Risks of Frontier Models for 3D Modeling, Computational Design and Robotics,” September 22, 2026; NVIDIA, “5 Steps to Create SimReady Assets for Robotics with Frontier AI Models,” October 8, 2026; Physical AI Podcast, “AI Models Fail 63 of 84 Robot Tasks, Waymo Borrows $5B,” October 10, 2026; Cableteque, “Cableteque Brings AI-Powered Wire Harness Quoting Platform to Europe,” September 29, 2026.\"}"}}
./runs/20261016T151820442758Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-78df1ed023d84e969b45e01f4f93ea25-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d\",\"version_id\":\"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is a fresh, timestamped commercial perspective relevant to physical AI as supporting context: NVIDIA Cosmos Lab VP Mingyu Leo discusses heterogeneous robot sensing at 00:12:37–00:12:48 and describes world simulation as taking current observations and action sequences to predict future outputs at 00:23:59–00:24:25. It supports only the attributed claim that NVIDIA sees open, adaptable models and simulation as important for physical-AI development; the sampled transcript supplies no reproducible evaluation, deployment result, or manufacturing-geometry evidence. Its claims therefore need model settings, task definitions, and independently observed simulation-to-physical checks to establish capability, but the speaker’s timestamped account is quotable and useful for interpreting the market direction.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-8786a3663d8c414d9bfbf6650fdc11b6-attempt-1.events.jsonl:5:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/\",\"version_id\":\"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"Although fresh and timestamped, this is general manufacturing-process reference material rather than evidence about frontier AI for 3D modeling, CAD, or physical-space systems. It makes no relevant, checkable capability claim about AI-assisted geometry, verification, or engineering workflows.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/\",\"version_id\":\"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This fresh, timestamped metallurgy explainer is outside the publication's lead topics and supplies no frontier-AI, CAD, or robotics development. Its general material-science claims do not change what an engineering leader could build on or verify with these systems.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/\",\"version_id\":\"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"The item is a current but general explanation of refinery operations, not a development in AI-enabled CAD, 3D modeling, or robotics. It contains no checkable claim concerning geometry, simulation-ready assets, or AI verification, so it is not relevant editorial evidence.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is a fresh, CAD-focused conference report with specific timestamped passages distinguishing existing Autodesk Assistant features from beta, Tech Preview, closed-beta, and planned capabilities. Its account of live demonstrations is useful evidence of what was shown, not proof of production reliability; the article explicitly preserves that distinction, especially for agentic PLM and connected-client workflows. As trade coverage of Autodesk's own event it is not independent corroboration of Autodesk claims, but it adds a commercial perspective alongside research evidence.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing\",\"version_id\":\"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"The fresh, timestamped vendor account is relevant to an adjacent engineering workflow: turning drawing packages into structured, reviewable BOMs and flagging compatibility gaps. Its 18-hours-to-45-minutes KCM Cable result is a vendor-reported single case with no disclosed dataset, extraction accuracy, error rate, or independent replication, so it supports only a claim to test rather than a verified general capability. It is accepted as commercial context, with human exception review central to the stated workflow.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/does-cableteque-quote-extract-boms-automatically-from-customer-pdf-drawings\",\"version_id\":\"6d917d47e8d4b52b9fe4f0290327adf5dea0f67fa26266abe25051ad74adc0af\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh and relevant in subject, but it restates Cableteque's own PDF-to-BOM and time-savings claims without a disclosed evaluation, error rate, conditions, or independent check. It is the same publisher and underlying product claim as the accepted Cableteque workflow report, so its repeated 96% figure is not independent corroboration and adds little novelty.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/losing-money-on-cable-assembly-quotes\",\"version_id\":\"33abdbe4f75624efed189d40297ade0c2f12f250f578435d87954b3c34d4693e\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"The article offers relevant practitioner problems, but its proposed solution and Resco turnaround result are vendor claims without disclosed before-and-after conditions, accuracy checks, or independent verification. It repeats the same publisher's BOM extraction, compatibility, pricing, and labor-automation claims already represented in the batch, so it is not novel independent evidence.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/retiring-estimator-quoting-knowledge\",\"version_id\":\"7684d3f81b48f399e04d30dd15d5c9125d3b3466ed41c07228ed6dc7b4631cc7\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"The operational concern is relevant, but the claimed platform capabilities and 70% turnaround improvement come from Cableteque's own account and a customer case with no auditable method or independent check. It also repeats the same underlying product claims as the other Cableteque items, rather than supplying a distinct practitioner perspective or new evidence.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/news/ai-wire-harness-quoting-europe\",\"version_id\":\"3f0b6128cabb2c363faca5fff7b5511c50c36083101892f525858da4428f081b\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This is a fresh company expansion announcement, but funding- or market-expansion-style news is not evidence that the AI quoting technology works. The stated EU hosting date, planned ISO certification, distributor relationships, and product claims do not include a checkable workflow evaluation; the latter repeat the same publisher's underlying product claim.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This fresh, timestamped survey directly addresses the lead topics and states its evidence boundary: 1,646 public posts across 707 cases were checked against available code, video, and documentation, while only 132 cases provide runnable code. It separates editable-scene and parametric-CAD benchmark results from untested tolerance and manufacturability claims, and separates simulation/controller results from withheld-condition physical validation. The survey is valuable research synthesis, though its aggregated claims remain only as strong as the linked case-level checks and it does not replace independent customer or working-engineer evidence.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_fresh.jsonl:10:{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh research-oriented survey directly addresses frontier models for editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, and robotics, and states its evidence scope: 1,646 public posts across 707 cases, with only 132 cases providing runnable code. Its strongest contribution is its explicit credibility boundary: benchmark and demonstration results support first-draft capability, while tolerances, manufacturability, withheld-condition transfer, and safe unsupervised operation remain untested or weakly tested. The compilation is not independent replication of every underlying claim, but it makes the distinction between evidence types and system harnesses explicit, providing a needed research perspective alongside commercial coverage.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_fresh.jsonl:18:{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282","decision":"defer","reason":"The episode is fresh and relevant robotics context because it discusses world simulation and the different sensor constraints of physical systems. But it is an NVIDIA executive interview, and the sampled automatic transcript supplies no checkable experiment, deployment result, disclosed evaluation conditions, or independently verified claim. Audio-confirmed passages plus released model, data, and transfer evaluation details would be needed before accepting it.","piece_ids":[]}
./runs/20261016T145228717481Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-revision-02-f1eaa63b895f4b9aaafa471297e22175-attempt-2.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"02\",\"title\":\"The Check Is the Capability\",\"question\":\"Which claims withstand scrutiny, and where are the evidence or interpretations in tension?\",\"argument\":\"This month’s strongest CAD evidence is bounded rather than general: Engineering.com’s Backflip tests verified mass agreement on two reference drawings, while the same testing exposed failures in a Fusion import and a multibody model. Across CAD, manufacturing quoting, and robotics simulation, the products increasingly create structured engineering outputs, but their stated checks address different risks. Engineering leaders should make geometry, feature history, BOM completeness, manufacturability, simulation behavior, and hardware transfer separate acceptance gates.\",\"synthesis\":\"The sources describe a stack of increasingly consequential checks. Engineering.com’s Backflip reporting establishes mass agreement for particular STEP outputs; Cableteque describes compatibility-based flags for estimator review; NVIDIA describes visual, physics, and simulated grasp checks; and the MIT-CDFG survey distinguishes editable CAD outputs from tolerance and manufacturability validation. Together, they show that a usable generated artifact is not one capability but several: passing one layer should advance an artifact to the next check, not certify it for production.\",\"limitations\":\"Backflip’s reported mass checks cover two reference exercises, not tolerance conformance, feature-history transfer, assembly completeness, or fabricated-part results. Cableteque, NVIDIA, and Onshape describe their own products; the accepted evidence does not provide independent error rates, representative test sets, or physical production outcomes for their workflows. Customer and working-engineer evidence remains limited.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"02-c1\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip’s first tested drawing-to-CAD output matched the reference mass after the reporter checked its downloaded STEP file in Fusion.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"download a STEP file\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Backflip got it exactly correct.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c2\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip also passed its mass test on a second, more difficult TooTallToby drawing.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"a more difficult challenge\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Backflip aced the test.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c3\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip’s Fusion add-in only partially recreated geometry for one tested drawing.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"only partially recreated the geometry\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c4\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip created one body rather than all seven bodies for a multibody wire shelf.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"only created one of the seven bodies\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c5\",\"statement\":\"Cableteque says its software produces a structured, priceable BOM from customer drawing packages.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing\",\"version_id\":\"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"produces a structured, priceable BOM\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c6\",\"statement\":\"Cableteque says it flags likely-missing terminals, seals, and cavity plugs based on connector-and-wire compatibility.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing\",\"version_id\":\"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"flags likely-missing terminals, seals and cavity plugs\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing\",\"version_id\":\"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"based on connector and wire compatibility\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c7\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA describes a workflow that checks an imported robot’s scale, parts, and appearance against references.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c8\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA describes configuring joints and collision geometry, then rerunning simulation-ready and grasp checks after fixes.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c9\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA’s described asset workflow ends with testing a sequence in Isaac Sim, so it supports simulated behavior rather than a claim of physical-hardware transfer.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"checked before deployment\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c10\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says its Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails and currently applies only to public documents.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"public documents only\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"02-c11\",\"statement\":\"The MIT-CDFG survey concludes that frontier models are effective drafting tools for 3D and CAD work, while manufacturability requires further evaluation.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"effective drafting tools for 3D and CAD work\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"manufacturability requires further evaluation\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-03-694574ae4cb541a89408c610eda766ae-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"03\",\"title\":\"From AI CAD Demos to Governable Workflows\",\"question\":\"What do these developments imply for the audience, and what should they watch next?\",\"argument\":\"Technical leaders should treat frontier AI as a useful first-draft and workflow-assistance layer in CAD, not as an autonomous engineering authority. The near-term opportunity is to test bounded tasks with explicit checks—such as geometry import, mass, visual properties, collision geometry, and grasp behavior—while retaining human approval for tolerances, manufacturability, and production changes. The key signal to watch is whether vendors publish repeatable results under the checks that downstream engineering decisions actually require.\",\"synthesis\":\"The evidence connects a practitioner’s exact-mass check of two drawing-to-CAD outputs with a survey’s warning that current CAD benchmarks do not test physical tolerances or manufacturability. Autodesk’s connected-workflow direction and Onshape’s narrowly scoped public-document search show that vendors are moving AI into engineering information flows, while Nvidia’s workflow distinguishes visual, physics, and simulation checks rather than collapsing them into a single “sim-ready” label. The resulting editorial judgment is that adoption should be organized around staged verification gates and permissions, because a valid CAD artifact or successful simulation step is not evidence that an engineering change is ready to release.\",\"limitations\":\"The strongest direct CAD test here covers two constrained benchmark-style drawings and one practitioner’s workflow; it does not establish performance on production drawings, assemblies, tolerance requirements, or manufacturing outcomes. Vendor demonstrations and product announcements establish availability or intended workflows, not independent reliability in private engineering environments.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"03-c1\",\"statement\":\"In a practitioner test, Backflip STEP outputs matched the specified mass for two TooTallToby drawing challenges after import into Fusion and material assignment.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"I was able to import it into Fusion, apply the material, and check the mass.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"I can verify that Backflip got it exactly correct.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"once again, Backflip aced the test.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c2\",\"statement\":\"That same test found that Backflip created only one of seven bodies for a multibody wire-shelf drawing.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"it only created one of the seven bodies\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c3\",\"statement\":\"Current public evidence supports using frontier models as first-draft CAD tools, but does not establish conformance to tolerances or manufacturability.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"reliable enough to serve as first drafts\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"We may have been simplistic\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c4\",\"statement\":\"Onshape’s AI-generated thumbnail-description search is an opt-in Labs feature limited to public documents.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"You have to opt in and enable it\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"It applies to public documents only\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c5\",\"statement\":\"A CAD-to-simulation workflow should separately check visual properties, physics properties, and selected simulation behavior before treating an asset as ready for simulation.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c6\",\"statement\":\"Autodesk’s AU demonstrations included an agentic PLM workflow that identified an approved substitute part and prepared a change order, but the article distinguishes demonstrations from production availability.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"found an approved substitute part, and prepared a change order\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Some are in beta or Tech Preview\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c7\",\"statement\":\"Robot-control evidence reinforces the need for outcome-based gates: in one reported simulation evaluation, no model solved 63 of 84 tasks.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0047\"}},{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0236\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261016T151820442758Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-39726da32b174b68831401c847ec6ac5-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This recent, directly relevant survey addresses editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, manufacturing limits, and robotics, and provides quotable passages plus a September 22 timestamp. Its credibility is bounded by its stated checks: it indexes 1,646 public posts across 707 cases and reports checking available code, videos, and documentation, while acknowledging that only 132 cases have runnable code and most results are demonstrations rather than independent reproductions. It is valuable for the tension between benchmarked CAD/scene results and untested tolerances, dimensions, manufacturability, and withheld-condition physical transfer; its aggregate findings should not be treated as independent corroboration of the underlying vendor claims.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_reviewed.jsonl:10:{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh research-oriented survey directly addresses frontier models for editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, and robotics, and states its evidence scope: 1,646 public posts across 707 cases, with only 132 cases providing runnable code. Its strongest contribution is its explicit credibility boundary: benchmark and demonstration results support first-draft capability, while tolerances, manufacturability, withheld-condition transfer, and safe unsupervised operation remain untested or weakly tested. The compilation is not independent replication of every underlying claim, but it makes the distinction between evidence types and system harnesses explicit, providing a needed research perspective alongside commercial coverage.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/decisions_reviewed.jsonl:18:{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282","decision":"defer","reason":"The episode is fresh and relevant robotics context because it discusses world simulation and the different sensor constraints of physical systems. But it is an NVIDIA executive interview, and the sampled automatic transcript supplies no checkable experiment, deployment result, disclosed evaluation conditions, or independently verified claim. Audio-confirmed passages plus released model, data, and transfer evaluation details would be needed before accepting it.","piece_ids":[]}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-01-1a8d23c139784c8e9c85a37c32f325fa-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD AI Is Moving Into Workflows—But Its Checks Still Define Its Value\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"This month’s meaningful change is not that AI can generate geometry, but that it is entering recognizable CAD workflows: reconstructing some constrained parts, making visual model attributes searchable, and connecting design data across applications. The strongest evidence supports first-draft and retrieval uses with bounded checks, not autonomous engineering decisions. For technical leaders, the near-term opportunity is to adopt AI where a downstream CAD, geometry, or workflow check can reject errors before release.\",\"synthesis\":\"Independent evidence points to a common shift from isolated generation demos toward tool-connected CAD work. Engineering.com tested exported CAD against a specified-material mass check; Onshape made thumbnail-derived descriptions searchable in public documents; and Autodesk demonstrated connected workflows while explicitly separating available capabilities from previews. Together, these show practical movement in generation, discovery, and orchestration—but the tests differ: mass verifies a constrained benchmark artifact, thumbnail search verifies neither geometry nor engineering intent, and a live demo verifies only that a demonstrated workflow ran under unstated conditions. The analysis adds a deployment boundary: use these systems where the organization can define a matching acceptance check and retain human approval for changes with manufacturing or operational consequences.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence does not establish dependable performance on production drawings, tolerances, manufacturability, private engineering repositories, or end-to-end change approval. The strongest reconstruction result is a single practitioner’s two successful benchmark-style tests, while Autodesk and Onshape evidence is primarily vendor or event reporting rather than independent deployment evidence.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"A practitioner imported two Backflip drawing-to-CAD STEP outputs into Fusion, applied the specified material, and found each had the exact required mass; the same test failed on a seven-body drawing because Backflip created only one body.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"verify that Backflip got it exactly correct\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"only created one of the seven bodies\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says its opt-in Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from static model thumbnails, and it currently applies only to public documents.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"currently applies to public documents\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"Autodesk University coverage described Fusion agentic-PLM and connected CAD workflows as a mixture of current capabilities, beta or Tech Preview features, and longer-term plans.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Some are in beta or Tech Preview\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"identified the potential impact\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"For CAD teams, the defensible near-term adoption pattern is to use AI for first drafts or retrieval only when a task-appropriate downstream check and approval process can catch errors.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"apply the material and check the mass\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0036\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-revision-01-7c9632c597914c3b83383ee67c5a0599-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD AI Is Moving Into Workflows—But Its Checks Still Define Its Value\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"This month’s meaningful change is not simply AI-generated geometry, but its entry into recognizable CAD workflows: reconstructing some constrained parts, making model appearances searchable, and linking design data across applications. The strongest evidence supports bounded first-draft and retrieval uses, not autonomous engineering decisions. For technical leaders, the near-term opportunity is to deploy AI where a matching CAD, geometry, or workflow check can reject errors before release.\",\"synthesis\":\"The evidence shows movement from isolated generation toward tool-connected CAD work, but with sharply different validation boundaries. Engineering.com used a specified-material mass check on two exported CAD outputs; Onshape describes searchable text derived from model thumbnails in public documents; and Cadalyst reports that Autodesk’s connected-workflow announcements span available, preview, and planned functions. Nvidia’s sim-ready workflow similarly separates visual, physics, and grasp checks, while robotics reporting shows why a completed action sequence is not itself evidence of task success. The resulting editorial conclusion is that adoption readiness depends less on whether a model produces an artifact than on whether the organization has an acceptance check that matches the consequence of using it.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence does not establish dependable performance on production drawings, tolerances, manufacturability, private engineering repositories, or end-to-end change approval. Backflip’s strongest reconstruction evidence comes from one practitioner’s two successful benchmark-style mass checks; Onshape and Autodesk provide vendor or event-reporting evidence rather than independent production-deployment results. The robotics evidence is supporting context, not proof that CAD-generated or simulation-ready assets transfer reliably to hardware.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"A practitioner reported that two Backflip drawing-to-CAD STEP outputs matched the required mass after material assignment in Fusion, while Backflip produced only one body for a seven-body drawing.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"apply the material and check the mass\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"verify that Backflip got it exactly correct\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"once again, Backflip aced the test\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"only created one of the seven bodies\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says its opt-in Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from static model thumbnails and currently applies only to public documents.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"currently applies to public documents\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"Cadalyst reported that Autodesk showed developing Fusion agentic-PLM capabilities and distinguished current capabilities from beta, Tech Preview, and longer-term work.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Fusion’s developing agentic PLM capabilities\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Some are in beta or Tech Preview\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"longer-term direction\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"For CAD teams, the defensible near-term adoption pattern is to use AI for first drafts or retrieval only when a task-appropriate downstream check and approval process can catch errors.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"apply the material and check the mass\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0036\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261016T025435190699Z/briefs_editorial.jsonl:1:{"piece_id":"01","title":"CAD AI Is Moving Into Workflows—But Its Checks Still Define Its Value","question":"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?","argument":"This month’s meaningful change is not simply AI-generated geometry, but its entry into recognizable CAD workflows: reconstructing some constrained parts, making model appearances searchable, and linking design data across applications. The strongest evidence supports bounded first-draft and retrieval uses, not autonomous engineering decisions. For technical leaders, the near-term opportunity is to deploy AI where a matching CAD, geometry, or workflow check can reject errors before release. A wire-harness quoting startup also announced European availability, but that is a market signal, not a verified accuracy result.","synthesis":"The evidence shows movement from isolated generation toward tool-connected CAD work, but with sharply different validation boundaries. Engineering.com used a specified-material mass check on two exported CAD outputs; Onshape describes searchable text derived from model thumbnails in public documents; and Cadalyst reports that Autodesk’s connected-workflow announcements span available, preview, and planned functions. Nvidia’s sim-ready workflow similarly separates visual, physics, and grasp checks, while robotics reporting shows why a completed action sequence is not itself evidence of task success. The resulting editorial conclusion is that adoption readiness depends less on whether a model produces an artifact than on whether the organization has an acceptance check that matches the consequence of using it. Cableteque's announced expansion shows where drawing-to-quote automation is being sold, while its company release cannot establish extraction accuracy or customer outcomes.","limitations":"The evidence does not establish dependable performance on production drawings, tolerances, manufacturability, private engineering repositories, or end-to-end change approval. Backflip’s strongest reconstruction evidence comes from one practitioner’s two successful benchmark-style mass checks; Onshape and Autodesk provide vendor or event-reporting evidence rather than independent production-deployment results. The robotics evidence is supporting context, not proof that CAD-generated or simulation-ready assets transfer reliably to hardware. Cableteque's expansion and platform benefits are company claims without an independent performance study in the accepted evidence.","claims":[{"claim_id":"01-c1","statement":"A practitioner reported that two Backflip drawing-to-CAD STEP outputs matched the required mass after material assignment in Fusion, while Backflip produced only one body for a seven-body drawing.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"apply the material and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"verify that Backflip got it exactly correct"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"once again, Backflip aced the test"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"only created one of the seven bodies"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c2","statement":"Onshape says its opt-in Labs feature generates searchable descriptions from static model thumbnails and currently applies only to public documents.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search","version_id":"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search","version_id":"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"currently applies to public documents"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c3","statement":"Cadalyst reported that Autodesk showed developing Fusion agentic-PLM capabilities and distinguished current capabilities from beta, Tech Preview, and longer-term work.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Fusion’s developing agentic PLM capabilities"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Some are in beta or Tech Preview"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"longer-term direction"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c4","statement":"For CAD teams, the defensible near-term adoption pattern is to use AI for first drafts or retrieval only when a task-appropriate downstream check and approval process can catch errors.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563","version_id":"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"apply the material and check the mass"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-