./runs/20261016T151820442758Z/decisions.jsonl:9:{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This recent, directly relevant survey addresses editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, manufacturing limits, and robotics, and provides quotable passages plus a September 22 timestamp. Its credibility is bounded by its stated checks: it indexes 1,646 public posts across 707 cases and reports checking available code, videos, and documentation, while acknowledging that only 132 cases have runnable code and most results are demonstrations rather than independent reproductions. It is valuable for the tension between benchmarked CAD/scene results and untested tolerances, dimensions, manufacturability, and withheld-condition physical transfer; its aggregate findings should not be treated as independent corroboration of the underlying vendor claims.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
./runs/20261016T151820442758Z/decisions.jsonl:20:{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282","decision":"accept","reason":"This is a fresh, timestamped commercial perspective relevant to physical AI as supporting context: NVIDIA Cosmos Lab VP Mingyu Leo discusses heterogeneous robot sensing at 00:12:37–00:12:48 and describes world simulation as taking current observations and action sequences to predict future outputs at 00:23:59–00:24:25. It supports only the attributed claim that NVIDIA sees open, adaptable models and simulation as important for physical-AI development; the sampled transcript supplies no reproducible evaluation, deployment result, or manufacturing-geometry evidence. Its claims therefore need model settings, task definitions, and independently observed simulation-to-physical checks to establish capability, but the speaker’s timestamped account is quotable and useful for interpreting the market direction.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
