./runs/20261016T153413218193Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-revision-01-e9ecf504b7914239bf3d463df23bdded-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD AI Moves Into Engineering Workflows, While Verification Stays Separate\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"The important change is that AI is entering native CAD and simulation workflows through custom-feature generation, visual search, simulation setup, and drawing-to-CAD conversion. The evidence supports supervised use for first drafts, retrieval, and simulation preparation—not treating generated geometry as production-ready by default. For engineering leaders, the immediate decision is where these tools can accelerate bounded work while existing tolerance, manufacturability, and validation gates remain in place.\",\"synthesis\":\"The evidence connects a market shift with a verification boundary. Onshape and SimScale describe AI interfaces embedded in CAD workflows, while Engineering.com independently tested a narrow drawing-to-CAD case; together, they indicate that the near-term change is more assisted entry into engineering systems, not demonstrated autonomous engineering. NVIDIA’s simulation-asset workflow adds explicit checks for visual, physics, and grasp properties, while the MIT-CDFG survey identifies tolerances and manufacturability as still untested; the analytical implication is that teams should align each release gate to the specific property actually checked.\",\"limitations\":\"Engineering.com’s independent CAD test covered two successful speed-modeling drawings and one failed multibody drawing, not tolerance-critical shop drawings or production parts. Most remaining CAD and simulation evidence is vendor reporting about capabilities or workflows; representative internal test sets, disclosed failure rates, and downstream manufacturing checks are still absent.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip passed mass checks for two drawing-to-CAD STEP outputs after import into Fusion.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"I can verify that Backflip got it exactly correct.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"once again, Backflip aced the test.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Engineering.com reported that Backflip created only one of seven bodies for its multibody wire-shelf drawing test.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151563\",\"version_id\":\"90e3adc0a87a45dc20689ae62db7125fe378f8191522f5954fae4ace5e96c803\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"it only created one of the seven bodies\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says its FeatureScript MCP Server lets AI create, test, debug, and refine custom CAD functionality from plain-language requests.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/featurescript-mcp-server-use-cases-text-code-cad\",\"version_id\":\"9656a0a35f95ac0e0adb6ba1530e2759342633cbcecba8de9948699a032ab5a8\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"create, test, debug, and refine custom CAD functionality\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says AI Descriptive Image Search generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"generates searchable descriptions from model thumbnails\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c5\",\"statement\":\"Onshape says its AI Descriptive Image Search currently applies only to public documents.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.onshape.com/en/blog/ai-generated-thumbnail-description-search\",\"version_id\":\"b2755a997c3cdda71421bbdd40ee9721d353cbc20ed2f1f80e91169757b9bbd2\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"public documents only\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c6\",\"statement\":\"SimScale says its Onshape agent can propose a simulation setup, mesh and run physics, and report results in the Onshape environment.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151329\",\"version_id\":\"a5a6e64fd4f2a87b5b45be5afd0c01d19fd3ee1e8b8f12be9e7e49964e03d82b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"propose an appropriate setup, mesh and run the physics\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://www.engineering.com/?p=151329\",\"version_id\":\"a5a6e64fd4f2a87b5b45be5afd0c01d19fd3ee1e8b8f12be9e7e49964e03d82b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"report the results back in the same Onshape environment\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c7\",\"statement\":\"The MIT-CDFG survey says current frontier-model outputs can serve as first drafts but do not yet show tolerance conformance or manufacturability.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"reliable enough to serve as first drafts\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c8\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA says its CAD-to-simulation workflow checks imported scale, parts, appearance, joints, collision geometry, physical properties, and a grasp test before testing a full sequence in Isaac Sim.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c9\",\"statement\":\"The Physical AI Podcast reported that five general models left 63 of 84 robot tasks unsolved in RobotWorld.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/010\",\"version_id\":\"85cb287a2441351d8480acecc45d2ae3d6c8d1e3d180eee941a34d7bcda762d1\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c10\",\"statement\":\"Because NVIDIA’s workflow checks simulation-asset properties while the MIT-CDFG survey identifies manufacturability as untested, passing those simulation checks should not be interpreted as demonstrating manufacturability.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"manufacturability have not been tested\"}}]}]}"}}
