./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-01-8d7150b372f24054946725f122be2b1f-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD’s Shift Is From Isolated Authoring Toward Connected, Checkable Workflows\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"The most consequential change is not a single autonomous CAD capability but a widening set of connected workflow features: configuration propagation and assembly mass display in Onshape, plus Autodesk’s emerging cross-application assistant and connected-client direction. Frontier models are increasingly useful for editable CAD first drafts, but the available evidence still supports editability and benchmark task completion more clearly than tolerance conformance or manufacturability. Engineering leaders should therefore treat these developments as opportunities to improve drafting, context flow, and review—not evidence that downstream validation can be removed.\",\"synthesis\":\"PTC’s release record shows concrete CAD workflow features available in a native parametric environment, while Cadalyst documents Autodesk positioning AI and shared cloud context across the lifecycle, with important distinctions between available, beta, preview, and planned functions. The MIT-CDFG survey supplies the broader capability boundary: editable native CAD artifacts and benchmark gains are real advances, yet physical tolerance and manufacturability checks remain absent. Together, the sources indicate that the near-term change is a more connected and automatable design workflow around CAD artifacts, while engineering acceptance remains a separate verification stage.\",\"limitations\":\"None of the three sources provides an independent working-engineer study measuring productivity, mass-property accuracy, tolerance conformance, manufacturability, or the reliability of autonomous cross-system changes. Autodesk’s agentic PLM and connected-client demonstrations also include capabilities that remain in beta, Tech Preview, development, or planned status.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"Onshape’s October release says configuration inputs can be automatically propagated to reference Part Studios, assemblies, and Variable Studios, and that persistent center-of-mass display is available in assemblies.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0003\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0008\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Cadalyst reports that Autodesk demonstrated a Fusion agentic-PLM workflow that identified a motor-shortage impact, found an approved substitute part, and prepared a change order, while describing several larger Fusion automation and connected-client capabilities as announced or in development.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"In a demonstration of Fusion’s developing agentic PLM capabilities, for example, a motor shortage threatening production became a problem the system could work through inside an Assistant conversation. It identified the potential impact, found an approved substitute part, and prepared a change order.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Mixed. Autodesk Assistant capabilities are already appearing in manufacturing products, while several of the larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"The MIT-CDFG survey reports that models can produce editable parametric CAD parts and assemblies and improve on standardized CAD benchmarks, but that physical-part tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Models build parametric parts and assemblies, and solid models of up to 511 bodies, that remain editable in native CAD tools\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"On 100 FreeCAD benchmark tasks, the leading models average 85%, up from 70% for GPT-5.6 Sol, and fully solve about 45\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-01-e499e511fd384f5594c6258552088e70-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD’s Shift Is Toward Connected, Checkable Workflows—Not Autonomous Engineering\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"The meaningful change is not a demonstrated leap from prompt to production-ready part; it is the spread of connected CAD workflows that preserve parametric context, expose analysis and documentation information, and give AI systems more places to act. Onshape’s released configuration and assembly-analysis features show concrete workflow improvements, while Autodesk’s conference announcements point toward agents operating across connected product data. Frontier-model evidence suggests these systems are increasingly useful for editable CAD drafts, but tolerance conformance and manufacturability remain outside the checks reported here.\",\"synthesis\":\"The CAD product releases and Autodesk coverage describe an expanding operational surface: configuration inputs can propagate through parametric references, assembly center-of-mass information can remain visible and enter drawings, and connected cloud environments may let assistants span design and lifecycle data. The MIT-CDFG survey supplies the crucial boundary on that direction: native CAD benchmark and solid-validity results support use as editable first drafts, not claims that the resulting parts meet tolerances or can be manufactured. NVIDIA’s Newton presentation reinforces the same distinction for downstream robotics: simulation tooling can make geometry more useful in offline development, but a simulation demonstration does not establish physical transfer. The added analysis is that leaders should evaluate AI by the specific reviewable artifact and check it adds to the CAD workflow, rather than treating connected data, valid geometry, and real-world engineering correctness as interchangeable.\",\"limitations\":\"The accepted set contains no podcast evidence, so this provisional brief does not meet the series-wide podcast coverage requirement. It also contains no accepted, independently evidenced AI-native startup item suitable for Piece 01’s startup-watch signal; Autodesk, PTC, NVIDIA, and the MIT-CDFG survey cannot substitute for that requirement. Autodesk coverage is primarily conference and vendor-announcement context, and the available evidence does not independently test dimensional accuracy, tolerances, manufacturability, productivity gains, simulator fidelity, or sim-to-real transfer.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"Onshape’s October release states that compatible configuration inputs and values can be automatically propagated to reference Part Studios, assemblies, and Variable Studios.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0003\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"Onshape states that its persistent assembly center-of-mass display can show individual components or an entire assembly, with locations updating as components move and dimensions displayable in drawings.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0008\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0009\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0010\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0011\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"The MIT-CDFG survey reports that leading models average 85% on 100 FreeCAD benchmark tasks and fully solve about 45, while stating that tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"On 100 FreeCAD benchmark tasks, the leading models average 85%, up from 70% for GPT-5.6 Sol, and fully solve about 45\\n(Parametric CAD Bench 2026)\\n. Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"Cadalyst reports that Autodesk presented Fusion agentic PLM, AutoTimeline, AutoAssemble, and System Modeler as a mixture of existing capabilities, beta features, announced functionality, and development plans rather than a uniformly production-ready release.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Some of the capabilities Autodesk discussed at AU are available today. Some are in beta or Tech Preview. Still others represent a longer-term direction rather than something companies should expect to put into production immediately.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Elsewhere in the Fusion roadmap, Autodesk showed capabilities including AutoTimeline, which rebuilds an imported part's history so it behaves like a native parametric model; AutoAssemble, which tackles assembly creation; and System Modeler, which automates the CNC setup and production-planning work that is done before a part goes into machining.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c5\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA’s Newton walkthrough presents an open-source simulation engine and examples for robot simulation, but the accepted presentation does not provide a physical-transfer evaluation.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:4dbaTrlaLJ8\",\"version_id\":\"b92f49a0aeaa5497e59c4087239e6125670fea5992a0c80ba51d2162575d7ffa\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s1090\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:4dbaTrlaLJ8\",\"version_id\":\"b92f49a0aeaa5497e59c4087239e6125670fea5992a0c80ba51d2162575d7ffa\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0235\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c6\",\"statement\":\"For technical leaders, the near-term value is likely to come from deploying AI where outputs remain editable and can enter established configuration, drawing, analysis, and approval checks, rather than from delegating final engineering decisions.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0010\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Organizations still need to determine which project information an AI tool can access, who can initiate changes, how generated results are reviewed, and what constitutes an approved deliverable.\"}}]}]}"}}
