./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/eligible.jsonl:8:{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","kind":"podcast","media_url":"https://pscrb.fm/rss/p/dts.podtrac.com/redirect.mp3/media.transistor.fm/217445d3/e1eb0b6a.mp3","published_at":"2026-10-01T09:00:00Z","publisher_id":"changelog-media","retrieved_at":"2026-10-15T20:25:21Z","segments_path":"data/assets/podcast_b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d/a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282.segments.json","source_id":"practical-ai","text_path":"data/assets/podcast_b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d/a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282.txt","title":"Open models and the future of Physical AI with NVIDIA","url":"https://pscrb.fm/rss/p/dts.podtrac.com/redirect.mp3/media.transistor.fm/217445d3/e1eb0b6a.mp3","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282"}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-01-e499e511fd384f5594c6258552088e70-attempt-2.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"01\",\"title\":\"CAD’s Near-Term Shift Is Connected, Checkable Workflow—Not Autonomous Engineering\",\"question\":\"What changed, and which developments matter most to this audience?\",\"argument\":\"The consequential change is not that CAD systems have proved autonomous engineering, but that frontier-model workflows and mainstream CAD releases are making structured, editable design work more connected and easier to inspect. The survey finds stronger first-draft capability in parametric CAD, while Onshape and Autodesk show vendors moving configuration, analysis, review, and lifecycle context closer together. For technical leaders, the immediate opportunity is to evaluate bounded workflows with explicit checks and approvals, rather than infer manufacturability or production readiness from a valid model or a live demonstration.\",\"synthesis\":\"MIT-CDFG’s cross-case record distinguishes editable parametric output and fixed-harness benchmark progress from untested tolerances and manufacturability. PTC’s release provides a concrete example of the workflow substrate becoming more inspectable—configuration propagation and assembly center-of-mass display—while Cadalyst reports Autodesk positioning assistants and connected cloud clients across design and manufacturing. Taken together, these sources imply that the practical frontier is a verified handoff loop around structured CAD artifacts, not a single model replacing engineering judgment: the check observed is whether software can create, retain, display, and route design information; it does not match a claim that the resulting part meets physical or production requirements.\",\"limitations\":\"The accepted evidence contains no identified AI-native startup that can satisfy Piece 01’s startup-watch role, so this provisional brief cannot feature a startup as a feasibility signal. It also contains no podcast evidence; the series does not yet meet its cross-format podcast requirement. The strongest CAD capability evidence is a maintained survey that reports underlying benchmarks and demonstrations, while the vendor videos and conference reporting establish announced or released workflow functionality rather than independent productivity, tolerance, or manufacturability results.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"01-c1\",\"statement\":\"The MIT-CDFG survey reports that frontier models can produce editable parametric CAD assemblies, but says tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Models build parametric parts and assemblies, and solid models of up to 511 bodies, that remain editable in native CAD tools\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c2\",\"statement\":\"PTC’s Onshape release says configuration inputs can propagate to reference part studios, assemblies, and variable studios, while assembly center-of-mass display can update as components move.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0009\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c3\",\"statement\":\"Cadalyst reports that Autodesk’s Autodesk Assistant already exists in several products, while several larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Autodesk Assistant capabilities are already appearing in manufacturing products, while several of the larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"01-c4\",\"statement\":\"The evidence supports prioritizing evaluations that separately check editable CAD output, design-information traceability, and downstream engineering requirements, because none of the cited workflow checks establishes manufacturability.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0015\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Generating or modifying a design faster does little good if review, approval, data quality, or downstream production becomes the new constraint.\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/logs/editorial-create_briefs-sh-draft-03-5c7cec5a125f400a8a28982dcf5e1b8e-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"piece_id\":\"03\",\"title\":\"Build the verification layer; wait on autonomous CAD decisions\",\"question\":\"What do these developments imply for the audience, and what should they watch next?\",\"argument\":\"Engineering leaders should build durable CAD data, review, and verification workflows now, while treating agentic design and simulation features as assistive systems whose outputs still require domain-specific checks. The near-term opportunity is not autonomous engineering: it is making parametric models, configuration logic, approvals, and simulation-ready asset checks inspectable enough that emerging agents can participate without silently becoming the authority.\",\"synthesis\":\"The evidence points to a common operating model across CAD and robotics: AI or automation can move work across connected tools, but dependability is created by the checks around the handoff. Autodesk’s connected-client direction makes data permissions and approval ownership a CAD-management concern; PTC’s examples show that model robustness can be deliberately encoded in feature references and configuration propagation; NVIDIA’s prescribed CAD-to-simulation sequence makes visual, scale, joint, collision, and grasp checks explicit. The MIT survey explains why this distinction matters: frontier models can produce editable CAD drafts and valid solids, but the public record does not yet establish tolerance conformance, manufacturability, or safe unsupervised physical operation. This supports a build decision for verification infrastructure and editable native data, a selective buy decision for workflow features with observable outputs, and a wait decision for delegating engineering approval or physical-transfer claims to agents. No accepted evidence identifies an AI-native startup suitable for the required startup-watch role, so that element cannot be completed in this provisional brief.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence is dominated by vendor, platform, and survey sources rather than independent customer deployments or reproducible comparative trials. NVIDIA’s workflow establishes what its process checks, not that converted assets reliably transfer to hardware; Autodesk’s announced and previewed capabilities are not evidence of production performance. The accepted set also contains no podcast evidence and no eligible AI-native startup evidence, so the series does not yet meet its cross-format or startup-watch requirements.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"03-c1\",\"statement\":\"Autodesk University coverage says several announced Fusion, Forma, and Connected Client capabilities remain in beta, Tech Preview, development, or planned release rather than broadly production-ready functionality.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Some of the capabilities Autodesk discussed at AU are available today. Some are in beta or Tech Preview. Still others represent a longer-term direction rather than something companies should expect to put into production immediately.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c2\",\"statement\":\"Teams should build reviewable CAD governance before allowing agents to prepare or initiate consequential changes, because the Autodesk report identifies data access, action authority, approval, and generated-result review as organizational decisions.\",\"type\":\"inference\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"Organizations still need to determine which project information an AI tool can access, who can initiate changes, how generated results are reviewed, and what constitutes an approved deliverable.\"}},{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"quote\":\"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation.\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c3\",\"statement\":\"PTC’s Onshape release presents automatic propagation of compatible configuration inputs to reference Part Studios, assemblies, and Variable Studios as a mechanism for managing complex parametric designs.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0003\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI\",\"version_id\":\"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c4\",\"statement\":\"A query variable tied to a face can preserve the demonstrated ruled-surface update after an upstream slot is added, because the query follows the face rather than individually selected edges.\",\"type\":\"reported_fact\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:jLndwlduyzc\",\"version_id\":\"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0029\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:jLndwlduyzc\",\"version_id\":\"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0030\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:jLndwlduyzc\",\"version_id\":\"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0032\"}}]},{\"claim_id\":\"03-c5\",\"statement\":\"NVIDIA’s CAD-to-simulation workflow calls for checking visual properties, imported scale and parts, joint and collision configuration, selected foundation checks, and a grasp test before running a full sequence in Isaac Sim.\",\"type\":\"source_claim\",\"evidence\":[{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0004\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0005\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0006\"}},{\"item_id\":\"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw\",\"version_id\":\"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06\",\"locator\":{\"type\":\"segment\",\"segment_id\":\"s0007\"}}]}]}"}}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/logs/editorial-select_items-sh-d1e5c2667b2a4ae4abe07175f5e553ea-attempt-1.events.jsonl:4:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/\",\"version_id\":\"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"Although fresh and timestamped, this is a general manufacturing-process explainer rather than evidence about frontier AI for 3D modeling, CAD, or physical AI. It reports no AI capability, geometry workflow, simulation-ready asset, or checkable development relevant to the publication’s lead topics.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/\",\"version_id\":\"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"This fresh, timestamped metallurgy reference is outside the relevance criteria: it describes heat treatment but no frontier-model, CAD, geometry, verification, or robotics development. Its manufacturing context alone does not establish a useful connection to the editorial focus.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/\",\"version_id\":\"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"The item is a recent but general guide to refinery systems, not a development in AI-enabled 3D modeling, CAD, or intelligent physical systems. It contains no relevant capability claim or observed check that a technical CAD or physical-AI audience could assess.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams\",\"version_id\":\"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This is fresh CAD-industry coverage with a dated passage identifying Autodesk announcements around its Assistant, Forma, Fusion, and connected data, making it relevant commercial context for what CAD teams may be asked to evaluate. Its claims are primarily conference and vendor-announcement claims, not independently checked capability evidence; the report can therefore frame the change while Piece 02 should distinguish announced functionality from demonstrated dimensional or manufacturing correctness. As a single publisher’s show report, it is not independent corroboration of Autodesk’s underlying claims.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats\",\"version_id\":\"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"reason\":\"This recent, dated survey directly addresses frontier models in 3D modeling, computational design, and robotics, and its excerpt supplies a citable scope: 1,646 public posts and accompanying evaluations across 707 cases. It is useful research-oriented evidence because it explicitly separates public demonstrations and vendor reports from stronger evaluation, but its broad conclusions about verified solids and benchmark improvement must be traced to the underlying checks, settings, and graders before being treated as settled. It adds a research perspective alongside commercial CAD coverage, though customer and working-engineer perspectives remain missing.\",\"piece_ids\":[\"01\",\"02\",\"03\"]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:173f6c2b-e1b8-4de0-b7b7-4b15658d52e6\",\"version_id\":\"da6be0ed10587e503de7706e1ad94cd3d0409d0c4664a004a631d6f27c500a73\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"reason\":\"The dated excerpt is about narrative intelligence and general AI discussion, with no stated connection to 3D modeling, CAD, geometry, simulation-ready assets, or physical-system verification. It therefore fails relevance regardless of the speakers’ AI credentials.\",\"piece_ids\":[]}\n{\"item_id\":\"podcast:509842f7-f592-432c-