 podcast requirement. The robotics evidence is an NVIDIA presentation and establishes a product statement, not simulator fidelity or sim-to-real transfer; likewise, vendor workflow videos and conference reporting do not independently establish productivity, tolerance, or manufacturability gains.","claims":[{"claim_id":"01-c1","statement":"The MIT-CDFG survey reports that frontier models build editable parametric CAD parts and assemblies, while tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Models build parametric parts and assemblies, and solid models of up to 511 bodies, that remain editable in native CAD tools"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts."}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c2","statement":"PTC says its Onshape release can propagate configuration inputs to reference part studios, assemblies, and variable studios, and can display a persistent assembly center of mass as components move.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0004"}},{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0007"}},{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0009"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c3","statement":"Cadalyst reports that Autodesk Assistant capabilities are already appearing in manufacturing products, while several larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Autodesk Assistant capabilities are already appearing in manufacturing products, while several of the larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development."}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c4","statement":"NVIDIA says Newton is completely open source, a simulation-development signal that does not itself establish physical transfer for robot workflows.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:4dbaTrlaLJ8","version_id":"b92f49a0aeaa5497e59c4087239e6125670fea5992a0c80ba51d2162575d7ffa","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0489"}}]},{"claim_id":"01-c5","statement":"The evidence supports separately evaluating editable CAD output, design-information traceability, and downstream engineering requirements because the cited checks do not establish manufacturability.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation."}},{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0015"}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Generating or modifying a design faster does little good if review, approval, data quality, or downstream production becomes the new constraint."}}]}]}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/briefs.jsonl:2:{"piece_id":"02","title":"CAD Agents Can Draft More Than They Can Yet Prove","question":"Which claims withstand scrutiny, and where are the evidence or interpretations in tension?","argument":"The strongest current evidence supports frontier models as drafting aids for editable CAD artifacts under defined software harnesses, not as proof that outputs meet tolerance, manufacturability, or production-approval requirements. Autodesk’s announcements indicate a move toward agentic, connected CAD workflows, while NVIDIA’s process treats conversion of robot CAD into a simulation asset as the start of validation rather than its conclusion. The tension is between claims supported by different checks: benchmark completion, announced availability, and selected simulation tests establish different things.","synthesis":"The MIT-CDFG survey separates native-CAD benchmark results from untested physical-part requirements; Cadalyst separates Autodesk capabilities available now from previews and work still in development; and NVIDIA describes distinct visual, physics, and simulation checks after asset conversion. Connecting these sources shows that the appropriate unit of scrutiny is the model-plus-toolchain workflow and its explicit checks. A benchmarked CAD artifact, an announced connected workflow, and a simulated grasp test can each be useful evidence, but none by itself establishes toleranced manufacturability or reliable physical transfer.","limitations":"This provisional brief meets the three-independent-publisher requirement but cannot satisfy the startup-watch requirement because the accepted evidence contains no AI-native startup with a checkable claim; Autodesk and NVIDIA are established vendors. The accepted set also contains no podcast evidence, so the series-wide podcast requirement remains unmet. NVIDIA’s video describes a validation procedure, not pass rates, failure rates, or physical-transfer results.","claims":[{"claim_id":"02-c1","statement":"The MIT-CDFG survey reports that, on 100 native FreeCAD benchmark tasks, leading models average 85% and fully solve about 45 tasks, while tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"On 100 FreeCAD benchmark tasks, the leading models average 85%, up from 70% for GPT-5.6 Sol, and fully solve about 45\n(Parametric CAD Bench 2026)\n. Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts."}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c2","statement":"Cadalyst reports that Autodesk’s announced Fusion automation and connected-client capabilities have mixed availability, with several larger capabilities still announced or in development.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Mixed. Autodesk Assistant capabilities are already appearing in manufacturing products, while several of the larger automation and connected-client capabilities remain announced or in development."}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c3","statement":"NVIDIA’s video describes checking a converted robot asset’s visual properties, scale, parts, and appearance against references before later physics and simulation checks.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0004"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0005"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0006"}}]},{"claim_id":"02-c4","statement":"CAD-agent claims should be limited to the artifact or behavior actually checked, because the accepted evidence does not show that CAD benchmark scores, announced workflows, or selected simulation grasp tests establish manufacturability or physical transfer.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts."}},{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Some of what Autodesk demonstrated is ready to use today. Other capabilities remain in Tech Preview, beta, or the “coming soon” category."}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0006"}}]}]}
./runs/20261015T202519414242Z/briefs.jsonl:3:{"piece_id":"03","title":"Build the verification layer; wait on autonomous CAD decisions","question":"What do these developments imply for the audience, and what should they watch next?","argument":"Engineering leaders should build durable CAD data, review, and verification workflows now, while treating agentic design and simulation features as systems that prepare work for domain-specific checks rather than as engineering authorities. The near-term opportunity is making parametric models, configuration logic, approvals, and simulation-ready asset checks inspectable enough that emerging agents can participate without silently becoming the authority. This recommendation follows from evidence that current model outputs can serve as first drafts, while tolerance, manufacturability, and safe unsupervised operation remain unestablished.","synthesis":"The evidence supports a common operating model across CAD and robotics: automation can carry work across connected tools, but the confidence warranted by an output is limited by the check performed at each handoff. Autodesk’s report makes permissions, initiation authority, review, and approval explicit governance questions; PTC’s tutorial shows one face-based query workflow surviving one upstream edit; NVIDIA specifies visual, scale, physics, and grasp checks for a converted robot asset. The MIT survey supplies the boundary condition: editable CAD drafts and validated solids do not establish tolerance conformance, manufacturability, or safe unsupervised operation. Together, these sources support building native-data and verification infrastructure, selectively buying workflow features whose outputs and checks can be inspected, and waiting to delegate engineering approval or physical-transfer claims to agents.","limitations":"The accepted evidence is dominated by vendor, platform, and survey sources rather than independent customer deployments or reproducible comparative trials. NVIDIA’s workflow establishes the checks its process prescribes, not reliable hardware transfer; Autodesk’s announced and previewed capabilities are not evidence of production performance; and the PTC tutorial demonstrates one edit path rather than comparative robustness. No accepted evidence identifies an AI-native startup suitable for the required startup-watch build, buy, or wait role. The accepted set also contains no podcast evidence, so this provisional brief cannot satisfy the series’ cross-format requirement.","claims":[{"claim_id":"03-c1","statement":"The Cadalyst report says that some Autodesk University capabilities are available today, while others are in beta, Tech Preview, or a longer-term direction not ready for immediate production use.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Some of the capabilities Autodesk discussed at AU are available today. Some are in beta or Tech Preview. Still others represent a longer-term direction rather than something companies should expect to put into production immediately."}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c2","statement":"Teams should establish reviewable CAD governance before allowing agents to prepare or initiate consequential changes, because the cited evidence identifies data access, action authority, review, approval, and unmet engineering requirements as remaining control points.","type":"inference","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Organizations still need to determine which project information an AI tool can access, who can initiate changes, how generated results are reviewed, and what constitutes an approved deliverable."}},{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"These outputs are now reliable enough to serve as first drafts, but the record does not yet show that they meet engineering requirements such as tolerances, manufacturability or safe unsupervised operation."}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c3","statement":"PTC’s Onshape release says compatible configuration inputs can automatically propagate to reference Part Studios, assemblies, and Variable Studios.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0003"}},{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0004"}},{"item_id":"youtube:7i5XHQozfQI","version_id":"582b91bc01228116ecd2d1c461bae76ac4715fc7ed39fa319cf08c96874fdc2e","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0005"}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c4","statement":"In PTC’s demonstrated example, adding an upstream slot leaves the ruled surface updated with drafted faces and no errors because the query follows the face rather than individually selected edges.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:jLndwlduyzc","version_id":"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0029"}},{"item_id":"youtube:jLndwlduyzc","version_id":"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0030"}},{"item_id":"youtube:jLndwlduyzc","version_id":"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0032"}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c5","statement":"NVIDIA’s CAD-to-simulation workflow calls for checking visual properties, imported scale and parts, joint and collision configuration, selected foundation checks, and a grasp test before a full Isaac Sim sequence.","type":"source_claim","evidence":[{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0004"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0005"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0006"}},{"item_id":"youtube:H5UaOdIZERw","version_id":"c86fae4c3874c6aa997843fe5a3365bf0a32d21acb0927fbcea32b10e0709a06","locator":{"type":"segment","segment_id":"s0007"}}]},{"claim_id":"03-c6","statement":"The MIT survey states that no benchmark yet tests CAD tolerance specifications or manufacturability on physical parts.","type":"reported_fact","evidence":[{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","locator":{"type":"text","quote":"Tolerance specifications and manufacturability have not been tested on physical parts."}}]}]}
